From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: retain verified MT6878 display route

The PQ bypass graph leaves native scanout stalled at 1x1 with abnormal DSC
EOF. Selecting the exclusive retained LK PQ route on the same r151 kernel
produces a user-confirmed native interface. Acknowledged sampling with the
route held stable reports FRAME_DONE without new abnormal EOF events.

Apply that route in the DRM connect path so blank/unblank and session changes
cannot restore the broken bypass path. No diagnostic module is required.
The low selector fields identify RSZ0 rather than the parallel PQ bypass,
disable the unused PQ output CB4, and select split input zero. The full words
match the verified live transaction, including retained upper fields.

This is an explicitly partial bring-up change: flicker remains, and the PQ
processing blocks still depend on the documented LK handoff. It is not a
claim of independent cold initialization or completed display support.
Source definitions: Nothing OS 4.1 ee2be53cb75670b548948636a0db1d1ff112bf12,
mtk_drm_ddp.c. See docs/DISPLAY_FIRST_FRAME_AUDIT.md for the live evidence.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6878-mmsys.h b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6878-mmsys.h
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6878-mmsys.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6878-mmsys.h
@@ -31,9 +31,9 @@
 static const struct mtk_mmsys_routes mt6878_mmsys_routing_table[] = {
 	/*
 	 * Nothing OS chains all three primary 2-layer OVL blocks before the
-	 * DRM_BYPASS_PQ crossbars. OVL1 and OVL2 contribute no DMA layers in the
-	 * minimal pipeline, but they must pass the background stream and share
-	 * the display mutex with OVL0.
+	 * retained LK PQ path. Its RSZ/PQ initialization remains a handoff
+	 * dependency until these blocks have native lifecycle ownership.
+	 * OVL1 and OVL2 pass the background stream and share the OVL0 mutex.
 	 */
 	{
 		DDP_COMPONENT_OVL_2L0, DDP_COMPONENT_OVL_2L1,
@@ -58,9 +58,10 @@
 	}, {
 		DDP_COMPONENT_OVL_2L2, DDP_COMPONENT_DSC0,
-		MT6878_PQ_IN_CROSSBAR0_MOUT_EN, BIT(2), BIT(2),
+		/* Exclusive RSZ0 path; do not fan out into the unused bypass. */
+		MT6878_PQ_IN_CROSSBAR0_MOUT_EN, ~0U, 0x00010001,
 	}, {
 		DDP_COMPONENT_OVL_2L2, DDP_COMPONENT_DSC0,
-		MT6878_PQ_OUT_CROSSBAR4_MOUT_EN, BIT(1), BIT(1),
+		MT6878_PQ_OUT_CROSSBAR4_MOUT_EN, ~0U, 0,
 	}, {
 		DDP_COMPONENT_OVL_2L2, DDP_COMPONENT_DSC0,
 		MT6878_SPLIT_OUT_CROSSBAR2_MOUT_EN, ~0U, BIT(0),
@@ -81,6 +82,6 @@
 	}, {
 		DDP_COMPONENT_OVL_2L2, DDP_COMPONENT_DSC0,
-		MT6878_SPLIT_OUT_CROSSBAR0_SEL_IN, ~0U, 2,
+		MT6878_SPLIT_OUT_CROSSBAR0_SEL_IN, ~0U, 0x00020000,
 	}, {
 		DDP_COMPONENT_OVL_2L2, DDP_COMPONENT_DSC0,
 		MT6878_SPLIT_OUT_CROSSBAR2_SEL_IN, ~0U, 0,
